Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// This strategy targets chemistry answers that should appear inside visible
// << >> delimiters, with the molecule string itself governed by the parser.
// It tracks the visible generated output, whether we are currently inside the
// constrained molecular span, and the active constrained contents of that span.
// Outside the span it generates freely but watches for a naturally emitted "<<"
// delimiter; inside the span it uses parser-hard constrained decoding with a
// chemistry-friendly soft preference from validTokenGroups, and it can switch to
// a bounded multi-token symbol step when the parser state is not too narrow.
// This tracked state supports valid generation because currentConstrainedOut is
// the sole parser-governed prefix, delimiters control when parser authority is
// active, and every inside-span append is produced only by helpers that preserve
// parser validity.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the outside-span chunk branch, insideConstrainedOut stays
//   false unless UnconstrainedChunk stops on "<<"; then we call
//   EnterObservedConstrainedSpan, which sets currentConstrainedOut := [] and so
//   establishes a valid constrained prefix. In the close branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan exits constrained mode, making the implication vacuous.
//   In the narrow constrained branch, AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns either EOS
//   or a parser-valid next token, and AppendConstrainedToken preserves
//   parser.IsValidPrefix. In the wider constrained branch,
//   ConstrainedSymbolInGenerated returns currentOut that is a parser-valid
//   prefix, so assigning it to currentConstrainedOut preserves the invariant.
//
// progress: In the outside-span chunk branch, steps increases by stepsUsed and
//   UnconstrainedChunk appends at most that many visible tokens, so
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved. In the close branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan consumes one token-step and appends at most one visible
//   delimiter, so the bound grows by at most the incremented step count. In the
//   narrow constrained branch, AdaptiveConstrainedStep consumes one token-step;
//   EOS appends nothing, and a non-EOS token is committed by AppendConstrainedToken
//   with visible growth of exactly one, so the bound is preserved. In the wider
//   constrained branch, ConstrainedSymbolInGenerated consumes stepsUsed token
//   budget, possibly including EOS or rejected suffix tokens, while visible
//   growth is at most the consumed budget, so the output-length bound still
//   holds.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;
var narrowThreshold: nat := 12;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
